Mean of n number when each is divided by 5 is $\frac{x}{5}$.
Let $x_1, x_2, x_3, \ldots, x_nare the $number. \therefore$\text{ Given mean }=\frac{\text{ Sum of observation }}{\text{ Total number of observation }} \begin{aligned}
\frac{X}{5}& =\frac{\frac{x}{5}+\frac{x_2}{5}+\frac{x_3}{5}+\ldots+\frac{x_n}{5}}{n}\\
\frac{X}{5}& =\frac{1}{5} \frac{\left(x_1+x_2+x_3+. .+x_n\right)}{n}\\
X & =\frac{x_1+x_2+x_3+\ldots+x_n}{n}
\end{aligned}\therefore$ Mean of $x_1, x_2, x_3, \ldots, x_n$ is $X$.

